  "details": "For users who just have waist tracking, it’d be awesome to see it have a sitting animation instead of a crouch one, and a laying animation instead of prone.\n\nThe reason I say this is that at the moment, if a waist tracked user gets close to the ground (say kneeling or sitting down, their waist and head are in place but the legs and feet are extended far back behind them, making them look like they have ghost ectoplasm for feet. It’s funny, but it’d be cool to see it compensate for the lack of feet tracking to enable easier 3/4 body interaction.",
